{
  "produced_by": "voice_agent",
  "source_narration_script": "You have probably called yourself lazy. A coach named Gary John Bishop coached thousands of people, and he heard that word constantly. Underneath it, he almost never found laziness. They weren't unable. They just weren't willing. And calling it a flaw let them off the hook. So Bishop pushes a harder question. Are you willing to do what the goal actually costs? You want wealth? Are you willing to work eighty-hour weeks and risk everything? If your honest answer is no, that's not failure. That's clarity. Because willingness isn't a mood you wait for. It's a stance you take. Say I'm willing, and a door opens. Say I'm unwilling, and you draw a line. Both are power. What drains you is pretending. Refuse to act, and this is the life you chose. You have the life you tolerate.",
